    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_921de00f2727c102b99de664a98e69794da41e7140a435d18daa8b62d110536a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The functional-equation factorization first narrows the zero condition to a selected symmetric phase branch, whose cosine condition supplies integer-labeled critical-line ordinates; the displaced arg-zeta jumps then turn those labels into a staircase count. Comparing that staircase with the whole-strip count can yield saturation only after an independent global result that the regularized phase is well defined and has exactly one solution for every label, a premise the source argues for but ultimately acknowledges is not rigorously proved.",
