    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ae9fa29fe5d6930b482b03d80e07e40b099478d00b3eebd45059afb4182136be",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Neglecting arg zeta converts the average zero equation into a Lambert-W coordinate map that captures height and mean spacing; restoring the regularized argument displaces that coarse initializer onto individual known critical-line zeros. The source then tests what the added fluctuation preserves: phase-corrected ordinates reproduce the reported local pair-correlation pattern and sharpen truncated explicit-formula reconstructions of prime-count steps, whereas the smooth approximation retains only the density-scale backbone.",
