    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b77e8d1fd59d9702ea51b9b1cdc242fb6f4d81b072196b59b4be9648c489b073",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source validates its phase equations along several distinct on-line-data channels: root solving and substitution check pointwise numerical satisfaction, pair correlation checks retained local spacing structure, and explicit-formula reconstruction checks retained arithmetic oscillation. Read together with the final remarks, these results support the equations as effective encodings of known critical-line zero data but do not validate the separate global claim that one and only one selected solution exists for every label and exhausts the whole strip.",
